{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-81102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from the point $A(0,1)$ to the point $B(2,3),$ then ${\\int }_{C}{e}^{x}\\,dx-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi y}{2})\\,dy=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-81102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=j$ and $b=2\\,i+3\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =j+t(2\\,i+3\\,j-j) \\\\  & =j+t(2\\,i+2j) \\\\  & =2t\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x(t)=2t$ and $y(t)=1+2t$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=2\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{e}^{x}\\,dx-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi y}{2})\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi y}{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi y}{2})\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{2t}\\cdot 2-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (1+2t)}{2})\\cdot 2\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2{e}^{2t}-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi t))dt \\\\  & ={[{e}^{2t}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi t)]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[{e}^{2(1)}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi (1))]-[{e}^{2(0)}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi (0))] \\\\  & =[{e}^{2}+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})]-[1+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =[{e}^{2}+0]-[1+0] \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-81102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9fafabb0278ae60646c7f6d2c29ad1d8778cc51e06749c7198d7c30346c7fdc0"} {"question" "q-81102" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-81102" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "e+1"] ["math" "e-\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "{e}^{2}"] ["math" "{e}^{2}-1"] ["math" "{e}^{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-81102" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{2}-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,dx+xy\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the ellipse ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $A(2,0)$ to the point $B(0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $2$ and $1,$ respectively, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{x}^{2}\\,dx+xy\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{x}^{2}\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+xy\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}({x}^{2}\\,\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}+xy\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)^{2}\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}-8{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124651" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9fafabb0278ae60646c7f6d2c29ad1d8778cc51e06749c7198d7c30346c7fdc0"} {"question" "q-124651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "-6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "3{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124651" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{cos}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the path $C$ is the line segment $\\overset{―}{MN}$ traversed from the point $M(-1,0)$ to the point $N(2,4),$ then ${\\int }_{C}y\\,dx-x\\,dy=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=-i$ and $b=2\\,i+4\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =-i+t(2\\,i+4\\,j-(-i)) \\\\  & =-i+t(3\\,i+4\\,j) \\\\  & =(3t-1)\\,i+4t\\,j,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x(t)=3t-1$ and $y(t)=4t$ along the segment.\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=3\\,i+4\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}y\\,dx-x\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t-x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}-x\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4t(3)-(3t-1)(4)\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\,dt \\\\  & =4t\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4(1-0) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9fafabb0278ae60646c7f6d2c29ad1d8778cc51e06749c7198d7c30346c7fdc0"} {"question" "q-124654" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124654" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\frac{11}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124654" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If the path $C$ is a part of the graph $y=2\\sqrt{x}$ traversed from the point $P(1,2)$ to point $Q(4,4),$ then ${\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(x+y)\\,dy=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our curve is given by the explicit Cartesian equation $y=2\\sqrt{x}.$ As a result, we obtain the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j={t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j,\\,t\\in [1,2]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=2t\\,i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(x-y)\\,dx+(x+y)\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(x-y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+(x+y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}((x-y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}+(x+y)\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}({t}^{2}-2t)\\cdot 2t+({t}^{2}+2t)\\cdot 2\\,dt \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{2}t({t}^{2}-2t)+({t}^{2}+2t)\\,dt \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{t}^{3}-{t}^{2}+2t\\,dt \\\\  & =2{[\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+{t}^{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2[(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+{2}^{2})-(\\frac{{1}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{3}+{1}^{2})] \\\\  & =2[4-\\frac{8}{3}+4-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{3}-1] \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{53}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{53}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124664" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9fafabb0278ae60646c7f6d2c29ad1d8778cc51e06749c7198d7c30346c7fdc0"} {"question" "q-124664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "\\frac{42}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{49}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{53}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124664" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{53}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${\\int }_{C}dx+\\frac{2}{x}\\,dy,$ where $C$ is part of the ellipse $9{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=9$ traversed in the counterclockwise direction from the point $(-1,0)$ to the point $(0,-3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $C$ is an ellipse centered at $O$ with horizontal and vertical semiaxes of $1$ and $3,$ respectively, it can be parametrized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =x(t)\\,i+y(t)\\,j=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,t\\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now evaluate the line integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}dx+\\frac{2}{x}\\,dy & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{2}{x}\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(\\frac{dx}{\\text{d}t}+\\frac{2}{x}\\,\\frac{dy}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+6\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+6t]_{\\pi }^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})+9\\pi )-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +6\\pi ) \\\\  & =(0+9\\pi )-(-1+6\\pi ) \\\\  & =3\\pi +1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124665" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9fafabb0278ae60646c7f6d2c29ad1d8778cc51e06749c7198d7c30346c7fdc0"} {"question" "q-124665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\pi -1"] ["math" "3\\pi +1"] ["math" "3\\pi -4"] ["math" "4\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi +1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14076330/state.json" "file_sha256" "07ede299154df82020b74aeec12bb1156a7d56dcaec055d4deef0a51a158520c"} {"question" "q-124665" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\pi +1"